; Import stub for the system OpenCL.dll, for gpudecryptshellcode.py.
;
; This file contributes no code to any artefact. dlltool turns it into an
; import library so a mingw link can resolve the OpenCL entry points, and what
; lands in the image is one jump thunk per symbol - the implementations live in
; the OpenCL.dll a GPU driver installs, exactly as they do for a binary built
; against the vendor SDK.
;
; It exists because mingw-w64 ships no OpenCL import library and the corpus
; will not link the real one: KhronosGroup/OpenCL-ICD-Loader builds a static
; libOpenCL.a, and linking that would put the ICD loader's own several hundred
; functions into the sample under GpuDecryptShellcode's family name - the
; misattribution this corpus exists to prevent. OpenCL-ICD-Loader was also
; already ruled out as a family for the related reason that OpenCL.lib is an
; import library and the code never lands in a sample.
;
; The 21 names below are exactly the entry points GpuDecryptShellcode.cpp
; references, obtained from `nm -u` over its object file rather than copied
; from a header, so this list cannot drift wider than what the program calls.
; If upstream ever calls a new one the link fails with an undefined reference
; naming it, which is the failure mode to want.
;
; x64 only, so no stdcall decoration: CL_API_CALL is __stdcall on 32-bit
; Windows and the default convention on x64, and this recipe builds x64.

LIBRARY OpenCL.dll
EXPORTS
clBuildProgram
clCreateBuffer
clCreateCommandQueueWithProperties
clCreateContext
clCreateKernel
clCreateProgramWithSource
clEnqueueNDRangeKernel
clEnqueueReadBuffer
clGetDeviceIDs
clGetDeviceInfo
clGetPlatformIDs
clGetPlatformInfo
clGetProgramBuildInfo
clReleaseCommandQueue
clReleaseContext
clReleaseDevice
clReleaseKernel
clReleaseMemObject
clReleaseProgram
clRetainDevice
clSetKernelArg
